      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_City%2C_London",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area was farmland until 1908 when it hosted the Franco‑British Exhibition, sparking its development into a sports and exhibition hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_City%2C_London",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Streets in White City were named after countries that appeared in the 1908 exhibitions, reflecting its international roots.",
